---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import calendar from '../assets/iris/01_calendar.png';
import partner from '../assets/iris/03_partner.png';
import privacy from '../assets/iris/10_privacy.png';

const shots = [
  { img: calendar, alt: 'Iris calendar view with color-coded cycle phases' },
  { img: partner, alt: 'Iris partner sharing, a read-only dashboard for a partner' },
  { img: privacy, alt: 'Iris privacy screen, data stays on the phone' },
];

const jsonLdApp = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
  name: 'Iris: Period & Cycle Tracker',
  operatingSystem: 'iOS',
  applicationCategory: 'HealthApplication',
  aggregateRating: { '@type': 'AggregateRating', ratingValue: '4.9', ratingCount: '12' },
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Arbaz Siddiqui' },
  url: 'https://www.arbazsiddiqui.me/iris',
  offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
};
const jsonLd = [jsonLdApp, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://www.arbazsiddiqui.me/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Projects", "item": "https://www.arbazsiddiqui.me/projects/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Iris", "item": "https://www.arbazsiddiqui.me/iris/"}]}];
---

<Base
  title="Iris, a privacy-first period tracker"
  description="Every feature free, no subscription, no data sharing. Symptothermal-method fertility tracking, partner sharing, Apple Health sync, 12 languages. 4.9★ on the App Store."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  ogImage="/og/iris.jpg"
>
  <article class="narrow section">
    <p class="kicker">iOS app · live · 4.9★</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Iris</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A complete cycle-tracking suite built on a refusal. No subscription,
      no locked features, and no health data leaving the phone. The category
      leaders charge $60 a year and share data with third parties. Iris
      charges nothing and can't share what it never collects.
    </p>

    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>Platform</dt><dd>iPhone, iPad, Mac, Vision · <a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/id6761134901">App Store</a></dd>
      <dt>Rating</dt><dd>4.9★ worldwide · 1,000+ downloads</dd>
      <dt>Languages</dt><dd>12, from Japanese to Polish, 820 localized strings each</dd>
      <dt>Model</dt><dd>Free forever · optional $2.99 one-time to remove ads</dd>
      <dt>Data</dt><dd>On device; optional sync to the user's own iCloud. No servers, no accounts, no analytics SDKs</dd>
      <dt>Stack</dt><dd>SwiftUI · Swift Charts · HealthKit · CloudKit · StoreKit 2 · ~57K lines, 98 test files</dd>
    </dl>

    <div class="shots">
      {shots.map((s) => (
        <Image src={s.img} alt={s.alt} width={420} widths={[280, 420, 640]} sizes="(max-width: 640px) 90vw, 280px" loading="lazy" />
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Engineering notes</h2>
      <p>
        The prediction engine goes past calendar math. It learns each user's
        luteal-phase length, shifts ovulation estimates when an LH test is
        logged, and confirms ovulation from basal body temperature with a
        proper coverline and three-reading thermal shift. That is the
        symptothermal method, implemented honestly. There is a PCOS-friendly
        irregular mode that gives ranges instead of false-confidence dates,
        and contraceptive and postpartum modes that change the whole model
        rather than hiding a few buttons.
      </p>
      <p>
        The rest of the suite is included, not upsold. A colour-coded
        calendar and fertile window, ovulation and PMS phases, fourteen
        symptoms plus mood, discharge, sleep and weight logging, BBT charts,
        pill and hydration reminders, postpartum milestones, two-way Apple
        Health sync, partner sharing, PDF health reports for a doctor, and
        twelve languages. Every one of those is free.
      </p>
      <p>
        Partner sharing publishes a read-only snapshot through CloudKit,
        with no account and no server of mine in the middle. Reports render to PDF for
        doctors. Every feature works offline.
      </p>
      <h2>Growth, also automated</h2>
      <p>
        Iris markets itself. A content pipeline generates infographic
        posters with an image model, gates every one against a written
        creative contract (word caps, mobile-safe geometry, a diversity
        ledger so no two posts repeat a topic or a look), and publishes
        them as Instagram Reels, Stories, and Pinterest pins on a daily
        schedule. The App Store listing runs localized ASO: screenshots and
        metadata in eleven languages, produced by another pipeline. One
        person ships the whole stack: product, engineering, distribution.
        The full write-up is at <a href="/iris-pipeline">the Iris growth
        pipeline</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Links</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/id6761134901">App Store</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-title { margin-block: 0.35rem 0.8rem; }
  .lede { margin-bottom: 1.6rem; }
    .shots { display: flex; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 2.4rem; }
  .shots img { border-radius: 14px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .shots { flex-direction: column; } }
</style>
